# Engineering Change Workspace

Canonical lifecycle:

```text
Explore → Propose (Spec → Design → Approval) → Apply → Sync → Archive
```

Each non-trivial change lives at `openspec/changes/<change-id>/` and contains both OpenSpec artifacts and Harness governance evidence:

```text
change.json
context-pack.md
impact-analysis.md
context-impact.json
proposal.md
specs/<capability>/spec.md
design.md
tasks.md
task-plan.json
task-run.json (temporary per-task evidence, normally under evidence/task-runs/)
lesson-candidate.json
lesson-decision.json
approval.json
execution-evidence.json
review-evidence.json
self-refine-evidence.json
sync-evidence.json
archive-evidence.json
evidence/events.jsonl
evidence/failure-events.jsonl
evidence/lesson-preflight.json
```

Harness Engineering is the parent lifecycle; OpenSpec is its child
specification capability. `init_change.py` creates `change.json` with this
machine-readable relationship. Change-scoped OpenSpec operations run only
through `dispatch_openspec.py`; direct commands and `/opsx:*` cannot own change
creation, state, approval, implementation, Sync, or Archive.
`check_change_workspace.py` fails closed on a missing or altered relationship.

`task-plan.json` is the approval-bound parent DAG and `tasks.md` is its child
progress projection. After each successful task, run
`record_task_completion.py complete <change-dir> <task-id> --run <task-run.json>`.
It records the verified run and automatically changes the matching checkbox to
`- [x]`; Review rejects missing, premature, or manually drifted checkmarks.

If Apply is interrupted, keep the change in `IMPLEMENTING` and run
`record_task_completion.py resume <change-dir> --actor <agent> --json`. It
repairs the projection from validated evidence and reports the next ready DAG
wave. Existing source changes without a validated task run remain pending.

Use `init_change.py` to create it, `approve_design.py` to bind external approval to every contract artifact, and `methodology_state.py` to advance state. Never edit state directly.

Behavior specs use `#### Scenario`, `WHEN`, and `THEN`. Sync evidence maps every source spec to its canonical destination and matching SHA-256. Production scope also links an absolute production record path with the same `change_id`; Archive remains blocked until that record is `CLOSED`.

See `docs/methodology/core/change-lifecycle.md` for the complete phase and state contract.
